{title: 311 - I Would Be Like Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #311 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 311}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Earthly [Gdim]pleasures [G]vainly call me; I would be like [Am7]Je[D7]sus;
[D7]Nothing [Ddim6]worldly [D7]shall enthrall me; [G]I [D]would [G]be [A7]like [D]Jesus.
[G]Be like [C]Je[G]sus, [A7]this my song, [D]In the [D7]home and [G]in the throng;
[G]Be like Je[D]sus, [G]all [G7]day [C]long! [G]I would be like [D7]Je[G]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Be [Gdim]like [G]Jesus, [Am7]this [D7]my song,
[D7][Ddim6]In [D7]the [G]home [D]and [G]in [A7]the [D]throng;
[G][C]Be [G]like [A7]Jesus, [D]all [D7]day [G]long!
[G][D]I [G][G7]would [C]be [G][D7]like [G]Jesus.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]He [Gdim]has [G]broken [Am7]every [D7]fetter,
[D7][Ddim6]I [D7][G]would [D]be [G][A7]like [D]Jesus;
[G]That [C]my [G]soul [A7]may [D]serve [D7]Him [G]better,
[G][D]I [G][G7]would [C]be [G][D7]like [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]All [Gdim]the [G]way from [Am7]earth [D7]to glory,
[D7][Ddim6]I [D7][G]would [D]be [G][A7]like [D]Jesus;
[G][C]Telling [G]o'er [A7]and [D]o'er [D7]the [G]story,
[G][D]I [G][G7]would [C]be [G][D7]like [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]That [Gdim]in [G]Heaven He [Am7]may [D7]meet me,
[D7][Ddim6]I [D7][G]would [D]be [G][A7]like [D]Jesus;
[G]That [C]His [G]words [A7]'Well [D]done' [D7]may [G]greet me,
[G][D]I [G][G7]would [C]be [G][D7]like [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
